  "worked_solution": "First, we express $f(x)$ as a composite function:\n\n$$\nf=\\frac{1}{g},\\,g=\\operatorname{sinh}⁡s,\\,s={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nThe chain rule states that\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}g} & =-\\frac{1}{{g}^{2}},\\,\\frac{\\text{d}g}{\\text{d}s}=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡s,\\,\\frac{\\text{d}s}{\\text{d}x}=3{x}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, multiplying the three results together and substituting for $g$ and $s$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}f}{\\text{d}x} & =-\\frac{1}{{g}^{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡s\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{{sinh}^{2}⁡{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{3}\\cdot 3{x}^{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cosh}⁡{x}^{3}}{{sinh}^{2}⁡{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
